      en: "Taldykorgan is the administrative center of Zhetysu Region in southeastern Kazakhstan. Founded in 1868, it now has about 140,000 residents. It lies near Altyn-Emel National Park and Lake Balkhash. Economy is based on agriculture (fruits, grains) and light industry. The city hosts Zhetysu University. Architecture mixes Soviet and modern styles. It is an important road junction on the Almaty-Oskemen route. The Karatal River flows through the city. Significant infrastructure investments have been made in recent years.",
